# H3/H4 AI Strategic Sourcing Prototype — notebook

## Current status

- Next.js 16 prototype of AI-assisted supplier discovery for Stamping Services,
  styled with the vendored Tailoft design system (`public/tailoft/`).
- Supplier results render as full-width cards (`supplier-card.tsx`); a two-up
  tile variant (`supplier-tile.tsx`) exists but is not currently mounted.

## Key decisions

- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson, via agent): Added a "Contact Supplier" secondary
  CTA to the left of "Visit Website" on supplier cards and tiles. It opens
  `contact-supplier-modal.tsx`: a "Contact {Supplier}" dialog with a General
  Inquiry / Request Quote toggle. General Inquiry carries an inquiry-type
  dropdown; Request Quote carries description/quantity/date fields. Submission
  is simulated (confirmation state only) — no backend.
- Modals follow the existing scrim + card pattern (`gate-scrim`); forms use
  plain `<fieldset>` markup so Tailoft styles labels/inputs natively.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson, mock provided): Contact Supplier CTA styled as a
  tinted secondary — blue-10 fill, blue-100 text, no border, solid envelope
  icon. Tailoft's icon map lacks an envelope, so `globals.css` maps
  `l-icon[name="envelope"]` to the Font Awesome glyph (f0e0) the vendored
  fonts already carry.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): Multi-recipient quote requests show a
  "Sending to" row below Estimated quantity / Response needed by: gray-outline
  pills, each with a mini monogram tile (suppliers have no image logos) plus
  the name. Hidden for single-recipient sends. The old top-of-dialog chip row
  was removed.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The Project name field is auto-seeded by
  `buildProjectName` — first material + first process + part, title-styled
  (e.g. "Aluminum Progressive Die Brackets"). No recipient in the name (was
  briefly "… — NN, Inc.", removed same day). Editable defaultValue, same
  no-AI template rules.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The contact dialog is quote-only — the General
  Inquiry tab was removed. The project description is pre-drafted from logged
  answers by `buildProjectDescription` (pure template rules, no AI; bracket
  use case hardcodes "brackets" unless a Part type answer exists). The
  requirement pills moved into a closed-by-default Tailoft
  `details kind="accordion"` labeled "Your requirements (n)".
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The quote form has an Attachments module built
  from Tailoft's own `l-fileupload` (dashed dropzone, shows accepted types) and
  `l-filepreview` (name/size/remove slots). Files live in modal state only —
  prototype, nothing uploads. Accepted: .pdf, .step, .iges, .dxf, .dwg, .zip.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The contact dialog addresses multiple
  suppliers — `SupplierResults` owns the single modal instance and passes the
  recipient set (clicked card's supplier + all selected). Multi-recipient view
  titles "Contact N Suppliers" with a "Sending to" chip list. The selection
  bar's Request Quote button opens the same dialog on the quote tab.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The supplier-facing email lives on its own
  Gmail-style page at `/supplier-email` (was an inline preview in the dialog).
  Submitting the quote form stashes a `QuoteEmailPayload` in localStorage
  (`supplier-email-preview`), opens the page in a new tab, and flips the
  dialog to a compact "Quote request sent" confirmation with a "View supplier
  email" link. The page renders full Gmail chrome (topbar, search, compose,
  rail, subject + Inbox chip, sender row from Thomas <quotes@thomasnet.com>,
  Reply/Forward). Email body: buyer persona (Sarah Mitchell, Meridian
  Dynamics), light-blue quoted project description, requirements list,
  full-width "Not interested" / "View contact details" CTAs, reply-directly
  note, and a light-blue blue-text "Sent via Thomas on behalf of…" footer.
  Body copy says "through Thomas" (was Xometry). For multi-supplier sends the
  page shows the copy addressed to the first recipient.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): Request Quote form fields are Project name,
  Project description, a "Your requirements" chip list echoing logged
  left-rail answers (threaded from `SupplierResults` via the card), Estimated
  quantity, Response needed by, and a pre-checked required consent checkbox
  ("…agree to share your project and contact details") in place of the
  "sent directly" note.
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): The contact dialog's submit button is labeled
  "Send Inquiry" (was "Request Quote"). The results-footer button that opens
  the dialog still says "Request Quote".
- 2026-08-20 (William Johnson): A floating "Quick Contact" CTA (white pill,
  blue outline/text, sparkles icon) docks sticky to the bottom-right of the
  results list, above the Exit Agent pill. Clicking it opens the contact
  dialog preloaded with the top 10 ranked suppliers (`QUICK_CONTACT_COUNT`),
  bypassing the 5-supplier manual selection.

- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson): This `right-rail-*` clone adds a "Select
  Suppliers" rail (`select-suppliers-rail.tsx`) to the right of the results
  list: the top 3 ranked suppliers by name, an "Add to shortlist" secondary
  CTA (saves them), and a "Send RFI to Suppliers" primary CTA (opens the
  contact modal addressed to those 3). Hidden at ≤1024px.
- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson): Supplier cards are separated rounded panels —
  1px border, 8px radius, 12px gap and padding (was flush cards on a
  hairline-gap gray backdrop).
- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson): Cards dropped the "Contact Supplier" and
  "Select" actions; only Save and Visit Website remain. Contact flows now run
  through the rail RFI, the selection footer, and Auto Contact.

- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson): The rail is titled "Shortlist or Contact
  Suppliers" (was "Select Suppliers"). Cards swapped the Save bookmark for a
  "+ Add" secondary CTA left of Visit Website that toggles the supplier on/off
  the rail list ("✓ Added" when on). The rail auto-seeds with the top 3, which
  are also deselectable — dismissals are tracked so they stay off; re-adding
  restores them. Manual additions append in click order.
- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson): The capability pills row on cards became a
  requirements summary: green circle-check + "All X requirements met" (exact
  matches), "Y of X requirements met" (near matches, one answer relaxed), or
  "Matches your search" before any answers. `CapabilityRow` still exists for
  the unmounted tile variant.

- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson, reference HTML "Supplier Search 2a — responsive
  standalone" provided): Full layout rework to the reference's three-stage
  design, keeping Tailoft tokens/icons and the Canela display font.
  - Stage bar under the search header: 1 DEFINE ("N of M" questions) /
    2 EVALUATE ("X of 2,482 match") / 3 ENGAGE ("N selected"), columns sized
    to the panes below (280 / flex / 320).
  - Fixed-width define pane (280px desktop, 240px ≤1100px) — the drag divider
    and resizable split were removed. Pane restyled flat: 30px badge + serif
    15px header, hairline-separated question sections, single-column radio
    options, settled answers as tinted "✓ answer / Edit" pills, footer toolbar
    « / ← Back / Skip → / ↺ / ≡. The mobile bottom-sheet + swipe grip were
    removed.
  - Center column: title row carries a 230px location field (wired to the loc
    answer) + All Filters; answer chips are compact single pills with the
    label inside (PROCESS Progressive Die ✕). Cards are flat rows separated
    by hairlines (supersedes the rounded-panel look from earlier today):
    46px bordered monogram, dot-joined facts line ("City, ST ZIP · N
    employees · $rev · Est. year"), semibold types line, description with
    more+, and the requirements summary as a bordered pill with a solid green
    circle check. Card CTAs are 36px.
  - Engage rail (320px): "Shortlist & contact suppliers" header with
    paper-plane badge and subcopy, removable entries (28px monogram, name,
    location, ✕), "+ Add to shortlist", "Send RFI to N Suppliers", and the
    Auto Contact CTA moved in from the floating dock (dashed tinted button).
    The floating Quick Contact pill and the dark selection footer were
    removed; `SupplierResults` reports the rail count up via
    `onRailCountChange` for the stage bar.
  - Responsive per the reference: ≤1100px hides the rail and shows a fixed
    bottom engage tray (avatar stack, "N suppliers to engage", Send RFI);
    ≤699px hides the stage bar/nav links/location for mobile tabs
    (1 Define / 2 Evaluate / 3 Engage · N) that swap the single column, a
    ✦ Refine tray button jumping back to Define, and a compact card variant
    (38px logo, +Add only, Visit Website as a foot-row link, media hidden).

- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson, follow-ups): results header scoped to the
  center column only (no longer runs over the engage rail — header + list now
  wrapped in `.results-center` beside the rail); define pane header retitled
  "Smart filter your search"; define option rows bumped to 13px text.

- 2026-08-27 (William Johnson, later tweaks): type sizes — rail CTAs 15px,
